# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Vite + React project following the latest official documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) using npm
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json` with the new dependency

### 2. Analytics Integration
**Modified: `frontend/src/App.tsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'`
- Placed `<Analytics />` component at the end of the App component's JSX, after the Routes component
- This follows the official Vercel documentation for React/Vite applications

### 3. Implementation Details
According to the Vercel Web Analytics documentation fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart:
- For Vite/React projects, the `<Analytics />` component from `@vercel/analytics/react` should be added to the main App component
- The component is placed after the main content to ensure proper page view tracking
- No additional configuration is required - the component will automatically start tracking once deployed to Vercel

## Verification Steps Completed
✅ Build test passed: `npm run build` completed successfully with no errors
✅ Linter checked: No new errors introduced by the Analytics integration (pre-existing linting issues in other files remain unchanged)
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ Package dependencies installed and lock files updated

## Deployment Notes
- Web Analytics must be enabled in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section) for the project
- Once deployed, analytics data will be collected automatically
- Verify functionality in production by checking browser Network tab for requests to the analytics endpoint

## Files Modified
1. `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
2. `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies
3. `frontend/src/App.tsx` - Added Analytics component import and usage
